Split-License Router
====================

Copyright (c) 2026 pink-kitsune-420

This monorepo contains MIT-licensed engine software and proprietary game
materials. The MIT grant below applies only to the engine scope. Both
complete license texts follow this router; a bundled copy of this file as
LICENSE.txt carries the same scope and terms.

MIT ENGINE SCOPE

The core Spacelab Engine in packages/* and modules/*, its public APIs
(including packages/game-api), reusable rendering, physics, editor tools,
shared libraries and generic host runners are MIT-licensed, except for the
explicit proprietary artwork definition identified below. Commercial use,
modification and redistribution of the engine and APIs are permitted under
the MIT terms. Game-specific code is not a generic host runner merely
because it is stored in apps/web/src/.

PROPRIETARY GAME SCOPE — ALL RIGHTS RESERVED

All apps/web/src/successor-*.ts files and the following paths are covered:

  games/space-sim/**
  games/space-sim-successor/**
  apps/web/src/academy-flight.ts
  apps/web/src/bundled-games.ts
  apps/web/src/default-launch.ts
  apps/web/src/flight-host.ts
  apps/web/src/flight-manual.ts
  apps/web/src/flight-windows.ts
  apps/web/src/manual-content.ts
  apps/web/src/starter-product-format.ts
  apps/web/src/starter-products.ts
  apps/web/src/successor-air.ts
  apps/web/src/successor-comparison.ts
  apps/web/src/successor-focus.ts
  apps/web/src/successor-materials.ts
  apps/web/src/successor-overview.ts
  apps/web/src/successor-tile-demand.ts
  apps/web/src/successor-tile-patch.ts
  apps/web/src/successor-tile-store.ts
  apps/web/src/successor-tiles.ts
  apps/web/src/target-modules.ts
  scripts/starter-products.ts

Also proprietary: only the surveyLanderAppearance artwork definition in
modules/appearance-trainer/src/index.ts, as marked by scoped notices.
The module API, trainerAppearance, trainerArtwork and remaining module code
remain MIT; see modules/appearance-trainer/LICENSE.

The proprietary scope includes bundled Space Sim / Space Sim Successor
exports such as space-sim.spacegame, space-sim-successor.spacegame,
space-sim.spaceuniverse, their bundled universes/ packages and game assets
and products derived from proprietary sources. It applies to those same
materials in browser ZIPs, offline players, Android public/ assets, desktop
and server bundles, and release downloads, regardless of their location
or whether the original source directory structure is preserved.

LicenseRef-Project in these game files and package manifests identifies
the proprietary game license reproduced below and in LICENSE-GAME.txt in
each game directory. Non-commercial use, modification, public forks,
redistribution and hosting of original or modified games and assets are
permitted free of charge on the terms below, including complete builds
and free app-store releases. Selling or commercially monetizing these
materials requires prior written permission.

Other example games and deprecated games/space-sim-nextgen retain their
existing licenses. File extensions alone do not make independently
authored .spacegame or .spaceuniverse files proprietary. Shared engine
code and APIs retain their MIT license when used by a proprietary game.
Third-party components retain their respective licenses and notices;
see CREDITS.md and bundled notices such as NODE-LICENSE.txt.

